  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Foundation Wind Project I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project involves construction, erection, and operation of two (50 MW each) wind power firms In the Sindh Province of Pakistan. Both the projects will supply much needed power to national grid under 20 year take_or_pay Energy Purchase Agreement (EPA). Total cost of the two projects are estimated at US$ 280 million (US$ 140 million for each Project) and the capital structure envisaged for the Projects Is based on a Debt/Equity ratio of 75:25.</narrative>
  </description>
